Subject: [PATCH] Enable the existing mobile controls path under Emscripten

WHAT THIS IS
    A compatibility shim for the SuperTux WebAssembly build produced by
    .github/workflows/supertux-wasm.yml. It is applied at build time to a pristine
    upstream checkout; upstream itself is never forked or modified in place.

APPLIES TO
    Upstream: https://github.com/SuperTux/supertux
    Commit:   0c5f269c5b5b6559aa27f03682b6dcfb52ffb244 ("Pass argv[0] to PHYSFS_init")
    File:     src/supertux/main.cpp
    Verified still required on upstream master as of 2026-08-02.

WHY
    SuperTux already ships a complete on-screen touch control implementation
    (src/control/mobile_controller.cpp, drawn by ScreenManager, gated on
    g_config->mobile_controls). It is simply never switched on for the web build:

        #ifdef __ANDROID__
          g_config->mobile_controls = SDL_GetNumTouchDevices() > 0;
        #endif

    __ANDROID__ is not defined for Emscripten, so mobile_controls keeps its
    constructor default of false forever. It is additionally never read back from
    the config file (gameconfig.cpp reads only mobile_controls_scale and
    touch_controls_visible), and the Options menu exposes only the *scale*, not a
    toggle -- so there is no runtime or user-facing way to turn it on.

    Consequence, measured on a Samsung SM-A127F: menus are usable (taps reach the
    engine as mouse events) but no level is playable, because in-level movement
    needs held directional input and no on-screen controls are ever drawn. This is
    true in an Android WebView and in Chrome alike, so it is not an embedding issue.

WHY NOT JUST WIDEN THE #ifdef
    Reusing the Android condition verbatim would be a silent no-op: under Emscripten
    SDL registers touch devices lazily, on the first touch event, so
    SDL_GetNumTouchDevices() is still 0 at startup when this line runs. The browser's
    own capability flag is the correct question to ask on this platform.

SCOPE / SAFETY
    Touches one platform-detection line. It does NOT change gameplay logic, physics,
    rendering, the save format, or any behaviour on non-Emscripten platforms
    (the new branch is #elif on __EMSCRIPTEN__). It only decides the initial value of
    an existing configuration flag, on a platform where that flag was never
    initialised at all.

RETIRING THIS PATCH
    Drop this file if upstream starts enabling mobile controls for Emscripten
    themselves. The build will fail loudly (`git apply --check`) rather than silently
    skip if upstream edits this region, which is the signal to revisit.

---
 src/supertux/main.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/supertux/main.cpp b/src/supertux/main.cpp
--- a/src/supertux/main.cpp
+++ b/src/supertux/main.cpp
@@ -499,6 +499,13 @@
   }

 #ifdef __ANDROID__
   g_config->mobile_controls = SDL_GetNumTouchDevices() > 0;
+#elif defined(__EMSCRIPTEN__)
+  // SDL registers touch devices lazily under Emscripten - on the first touch event - so
+  // SDL_GetNumTouchDevices() is still 0 at this point during startup and the Android check
+  // above cannot be reused verbatim. Ask the browser for its touch capability instead.
+  // EM_ASM is a variadic macro and Clang requires at least one variadic value, hence the
+  // trailing 0 - the same workaround already used in PhysfsSubsystem::find_mount_userdir().
+  g_config->mobile_controls = EM_ASM_INT({ return (navigator.maxTouchPoints | 0) > 0; }, 0) != 0;
 #endif

   if (TTF_Init() < 0)
